{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and test setup, add a focused fix for stale requests, then run the existing tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nEvery request currently updates state when it finishes, even if a newer search has started. I’ll add a request counter that advances on every search, including clearing the query, and guard results, errors, and loading updates.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter. Only the latest search can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests.\n\nPublic API and normal behavior preserved. Tests unchanged; no dependencies installed.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; six inline race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. Commands exited 0.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter. Only the latest search can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests.\n\nPublic API and normal behavior preserved. Tests unchanged; no dependencies installed.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; six inline race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. Commands exited 0.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":15,"tool_calls":[{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"pwd; git status --short; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-m_m99ddq/1-1-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":424,"stdout_bytes":134,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-07f8b4ae504b7b15db384d29991f3214.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"grep_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test; git diff --check; git diff -- src/search/controller.ts","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-m_m99ddq/1-1-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":332,"stdout_bytes":2110,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-b9c819c7663c972671da76b9bd0fc473.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: 'new', title: 'New', url: '/new' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const timing of ['pending', 'finished', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('new');\n    if (timing === 'finished') { requests[1].resolve(items); await current; }\n    if (timing === 'cleared') await c.search('  ');\n    const expected = c.getState();\n    requests[0][outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? items : new Error('stale'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), expected);\n    if (timing !== 'finished') {\n      requests[1].resolve(items);\n      await current;\n      if (timing === 'cleared') assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n      else assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'new', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('PASS: 6 deferred-request race scenarios');\nNODE\n